Track 2: "Is the safety net fraying?"
- Story & Context: Elena, the lead trapeze artist of the Zampano clan, sat in the sound booth late at night while the Korg M1 hummed a melancholic melody, questioning if their union was merely a temporary patch on a lifelong wound. She stared at the mechanical diagrams of the high-wire rigs etched into the studio wall, the smell of ozone and stale circus popcorn filling the air. She realized that the music was the only thing holding their precarious history together, singing "I’m tracing lines where the rope begins to fray" as the bass dropped into a deep, hollow dub pocket.
