Track 3: Unraveling the Lion’s Knot
- Story & Context: Years after the wedding, the legend persists at the abandoned Lion’s Knot amphitheater, where locals gather to hear the "aftermath" echoes of that original night. A young performer named Marco found a discarded, hand-knotted stage rope left behind from the ceremony and used it to trigger a series of rhythmic loops on his sampler. As the crowd danced, the knot slowly untied itself on stage, an omen that the rivalry was officially dissolved into history, accompanied by the hook, "The knot is gone, let the golden threads unwind."
